From: =?UTF-8?q?Tobias=20Frauenschl=C3=A4ger?= <t.frauenschlaeger@me.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:22:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boards: nxp: frdm_rw612: fix swapped ENET PHY reset and
 interrupt pins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the FRDM-RW612, the KSZ8081 reset is wired to GPIO21 and its
interrupt output to GPIO55, as used by the MCUXpresso SDK ENET
examples for this board. The devicetree had the two swapped, so the
PHY driver toggled the interrupt line instead of resetting the PHY.
The KSZ8081 interrupt output is active low by default.

Tested with samples/net/dhcpv4_client: the PHY is found at address 2,
autonegotiation completes at 100 Mbit full duplex, and ping works in
both directions.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Frauenschläger <t.frauenschlaeger@me.com>
(cherry picked from commit e86092e44c7f0e16f5513ae79fec7f1ab592ff6b)
---
 boards/nxp/frdm_rw612/frdm_rw612_common.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/boards/nxp/frdm_rw612/frdm_rw612_common.dtsi b/boards/nxp/frdm_rw612/frdm_rw612_common.dtsi
index c346301132b..53cba86e2bd 100644
--- a/boards/nxp/frdm_rw612/frdm_rw612_common.dtsi
+++ b/boards/nxp/frdm_rw612/frdm_rw612_common.dtsi
@@ -232,8 +232,8 @@ mikrobus_serial: &flexcomm0 {};
 		compatible = "microchip,ksz8081";
 		reg = <2>;
 		status = "okay";
-		reset-gpios = <&hsgpio1 23 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-		int-gpios = <&hsgpio0 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		reset-gpios = <&hsgpio0 21 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		int-gpios = <&hsgpio1 23 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		microchip,interface-type = "rmii";
 	};
 };
